Anything executable in this directory is run after each announcement, with:

  $1  mode      boot | done | tick | approve | nag | escalate | idle | sub | err | bye
  $2  session   the project name
  $3  extra     done: "<elapsed>:<specialists>"   escalate: seconds blocked   else empty
  $4  ordinal   the session slot, 1-4

It is backgrounded, its output is discarded and its exit status ignored — a script here
must never be able to stall the daemon, because that would take every announcement with
it. Keep it fast and make it fail quietly.

Example: flash a lamp when a session blocks on approval.

    #!/bin/bash
    [ "$1" = approve ] || [ "$1" = escalate ] || exit 0
    curl -s -m 2 -X PUT http://hue.local/api/KEY/lights/3/state -d '{"alert":"lselect"}'
